{
  "id": "freertos-config", "version": "1.0",
  "name": "FreeRTOS Config & Heap Sizer",
  "blurb": "FreeRTOSConfig.h choices explained and the heap needed for tasks, queues and timers",
  "group": "embedded",
  "rooms": ["embedded"],
  "keywords": ["freertos", "FreeRTOSConfig.h", "configTOTAL_HEAP_SIZE", "heap_4", "heap size", "rtos heap", "task stack", "configMINIMAL_STACK_SIZE", "configMAX_SYSCALL_INTERRUPT_PRIORITY", "configKERNEL_INTERRUPT_PRIORITY", "FromISR", "interrupt priority", "NVIC_PRIO_BITS", "TCB size", "queue memory", "xTaskCreate fails", "stream buffer", "software timer", "cmsis-rtos"],
  "intro": "Adds up what every xTaskCreate, queue, semaphore, event group, stream buffer and timer takes from the FreeRTOS heap - stack, TCB, storage and the heap's 8-byte block headers, with the idle and timer tasks included - checks which interrupt priorities may call the FromISR API, and writes a FreeRTOSConfig.h. Sizes are for 32-bit Cortex-M ports of FreeRTOS V10.6, from the kernel's own structs.",
  "inputs": [
    { "key": "port", "label": "Port", "type": "select", "default": "ARM_CM4F",
      "options": [["ARM_CM0", "ARM_CM0 (M0/M0+)"], ["ARM_CM3", "ARM_CM3 (M3)"], ["ARM_CM4F", "ARM_CM4F (M4 + FPU)"], ["ARM_CM7", "ARM_CM7 (M7)"], ["ARM_CM33_NTZ", "ARM_CM33_NTZ (M33)"]] },
    { "key": "heap", "label": "Heap scheme", "type": "select", "default": "heap_4", "options": [["heap_1", "heap_1 (no free)"], ["heap_2", "heap_2 (no merge)"], ["heap_3", "heap_3 (malloc)"], ["heap_4", "heap_4 (merging)"], ["heap_5", "heap_5 (regions)"]] },
    { "key": "totalHeap", "label": "configTOTAL_HEAP_SIZE", "type": "text", "default": "16K", "placeholder": "16K, 16384 or 0x4000" },
    { "key": "cpuHz", "label": "CPU clock", "type": "number", "unit": "Hz", "default": "168M" },
    { "key": "tickHz", "label": "configTICK_RATE_HZ", "type": "number", "unit": "Hz", "default": "1000" },
    { "key": "maxPriorities", "label": "configMAX_PRIORITIES", "type": "number", "default": "7" },
    { "key": "minimalStack", "label": "configMINIMAL_STACK_SIZE", "type": "number", "unit": "words", "default": "128" },
    { "key": "maxNameLen", "label": "configMAX_TASK_NAME_LEN", "type": "number", "default": "16" },
    { "key": "tasks", "label": "Tasks", "type": "table", "help": "Stack in words (4 bytes each), as xTaskCreate() takes it. FPU = the task uses floating point (bigger saved context).",
      "columns": [{ "key": "name", "label": "Name" }, { "key": "stack", "label": "Stack words", "default": "256" }, { "key": "priority", "label": "Priority", "default": "1" }, { "key": "fpu", "label": "FPU", "type": "select", "options": ["no", "yes"], "default": "no" }],
      "default": [
        { "name": "control", "stack": "320", "priority": "4", "fpu": "yes" },
        { "name": "sensor", "stack": "256", "priority": "3", "fpu": "yes" },
        { "name": "comms", "stack": "512", "priority": "2", "fpu": "no" },
        { "name": "ui", "stack": "384", "priority": "1", "fpu": "no" },
        { "name": "logger", "stack": "256", "priority": "1", "fpu": "no" }
      ] },
    { "key": "objects", "label": "Queues, semaphores, buffers, timers", "type": "table", "help": "Length = queue length, counting semaphore max count or buffer size in bytes. Item size for queues only.",
      "columns": [{ "key": "kind", "label": "Kind", "type": "select", "options": ["queue", "binary semaphore", "counting semaphore", "mutex", "recursive mutex", "event group", "stream buffer", "message buffer", "timer"], "default": "queue" },
        { "key": "name", "label": "Name" }, { "key": "length", "label": "Length", "default": "8" }, { "key": "itemSize", "label": "Item B", "default": "4" }, { "key": "count", "label": "Count", "default": "1" }],
      "default": [
        { "kind": "queue", "name": "sensor_q", "length": "8", "itemSize": "16", "count": "1" },
        { "kind": "queue", "name": "uart_rx", "length": "64", "itemSize": "1", "count": "1" },
        { "kind": "mutex", "name": "i2c_lock", "length": "", "itemSize": "", "count": "1" },
        { "kind": "binary semaphore", "name": "spi_done", "length": "", "itemSize": "", "count": "1" },
        { "kind": "event group", "name": "sys_events", "length": "", "itemSize": "", "count": "1" },
        { "kind": "stream buffer", "name": "log_sb", "length": "1024", "itemSize": "", "count": "1" },
        { "kind": "timer", "name": "blink", "length": "", "itemSize": "", "count": "2" }
      ] },
    { "key": "useTimers", "label": "configUSE_TIMERS", "type": "bool", "default": true },
    { "key": "timerPriority", "label": "configTIMER_TASK_PRIORITY", "type": "number", "default": "2", "when": { "key": "useTimers", "equals": true } },
    { "key": "timerQueueLength", "label": "configTIMER_QUEUE_LENGTH", "type": "number", "default": "10", "when": { "key": "useTimers", "equals": true } },
    { "key": "timerStack", "label": "configTIMER_TASK_STACK_DEPTH", "type": "number", "unit": "words", "default": "256", "when": { "key": "useTimers", "equals": true } },
    { "key": "prioBits", "label": "__NVIC_PRIO_BITS", "type": "number", "default": "4", "help": "4 on STM32, 3 on nRF52/LPC/Kinetis, 2 on Cortex-M0." },
    { "key": "maxSyscall", "label": "configLIBRARY_MAX_SYSCALL_INTERRUPT_PRIORITY", "type": "number", "default": "5", "help": "Logical priority (as NVIC_SetPriority/HAL take it). ISRs at this number or higher may call FromISR." },
    { "key": "subBits", "label": "Sub-priority bits (PRIGROUP)", "type": "number", "default": "0" },
    { "key": "isrs", "label": "Interrupts", "type": "table", "help": "Logical NVIC priority (0 = most urgent) and whether the handler calls ...FromISR().",
      "columns": [{ "key": "name", "label": "ISR" }, { "key": "priority", "label": "Priority", "default": "6" }, { "key": "fromIsr", "label": "Calls FromISR", "type": "select", "options": ["yes", "no"], "default": "yes" }],
      "default": [
        { "name": "TIM1_UP (control loop)", "priority": "1", "fromIsr": "no" },
        { "name": "SPI1 (IMU)", "priority": "4", "fromIsr": "yes" },
        { "name": "DMA2_Stream0 (ADC)", "priority": "5", "fromIsr": "yes" },
        { "name": "USART2 (console)", "priority": "6", "fromIsr": "yes" },
        { "name": "EXTI15_10 (button)", "priority": "10", "fromIsr": "yes" }
      ] },
    { "key": "trace", "label": "configUSE_TRACE_FACILITY", "type": "bool", "default": true },
    { "key": "runtimeStats", "label": "configGENERATE_RUN_TIME_STATS", "type": "bool", "default": false },
    { "key": "staticAlloc", "label": "configSUPPORT_STATIC_ALLOCATION", "type": "bool", "default": false },
    { "key": "queueSets", "label": "configUSE_QUEUE_SETS", "type": "bool", "default": false },
    { "key": "newlib", "label": "configUSE_NEWLIB_REENTRANT", "type": "select", "default": "none", "options": [["none", "off"], ["nano", "on, newlib-nano"], ["full", "on, full newlib"]] },
    { "key": "notifyEntries", "label": "configTASK_NOTIFICATION_ARRAY_ENTRIES", "type": "number", "default": "1" },
    { "key": "tlsPointers", "label": "configNUM_THREAD_LOCAL_STORAGE_POINTERS", "type": "number", "default": "0" },
    { "key": "stackCheck", "label": "configCHECK_FOR_STACK_OVERFLOW", "type": "select", "default": "2", "options": [["0", "0 (off)"], ["1", "1 (SP check)"], ["2", "2 (SP + pattern)"]] }
  ],
  "examples": [
    { "title": "STM32F407 at 168 MHz: five tasks, queues, a stream buffer, timers; an SPI ISR above the syscall line", "input": {} },
    { "title": "nRF52832 (Cortex-M4F, 3 priority bits) with newlib-nano reentrancy and a tight heap", "input": { "port": "ARM_CM4F", "heap": "heap_4", "totalHeap": "8K", "cpuHz": "64M", "tickHz": "1024", "maxPriorities": "5", "minimalStack": "128", "prioBits": "3", "maxSyscall": "2", "newlib": "nano", "tasks": [{ "name": "ble", "stack": "512", "priority": "3", "fpu": "no" }, { "name": "app", "stack": "384", "priority": "2", "fpu": "yes" }, { "name": "flash", "stack": "256", "priority": "1", "fpu": "no" }], "objects": [{ "kind": "queue", "name": "evt_q", "length": "16", "itemSize": "8", "count": "1" }, { "kind": "mutex", "name": "twi", "length": "", "itemSize": "", "count": "1" }, { "kind": "timer", "name": "adv", "length": "", "itemSize": "", "count": "3" }], "isrs": [{ "name": "RADIO (SoftDevice)", "priority": "0", "fromIsr": "no" }, { "name": "GPIOTE", "priority": "3", "fromIsr": "yes" }, { "name": "UARTE0", "priority": "1", "fromIsr": "yes" }] } }
  ],
  "usage": "Give the port (ARM_CM0/CM3/CM4F/CM7/CM33_NTZ), heap scheme and configTOTAL_HEAP_SIZE (like 16K), the tasks {name, stack words, priority, fpu yes/no}, the objects {kind: queue|binary semaphore|counting semaphore|mutex|recursive mutex|event group|stream buffer|message buffer|timer, name, length, itemSize, count}, timer settings, __NVIC_PRIO_BITS, configLIBRARY_MAX_SYSCALL_INTERRUPT_PRIORITY and the ISRs {name, logical priority, fromIsr yes/no}. It returns heap used/free/suggested size, the per-block heap table (idle and timer tasks included), per-task stack notes, which ISRs may call FromISR, the raw BASEPRI values, and a FreeRTOSConfig.h (texts). Sizes are estimates for 32-bit Cortex-M FreeRTOS V10.6.",
  "sources": ["FreeRTOS Kernel V10.6.2 source: tasks.c (TCB_t, prvCreateTask order), queue.c (Queue_t), timers.c (Timer_t, DaemonTaskMessage_t), event_groups.c, stream_buffer.c; sizes checked by compiling with arm-none-eabi-gcc -mcpu=cortex-m4", "FreeRTOS portable/MemMang heap_1.c, heap_2.c, heap_4.c (xHeapStructSize, portBYTE_ALIGNMENT 8, end marker)", "FreeRTOS portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c (vPortValidateInterruptPriority, PRIGROUP and configMAX_SYSCALL_INTERRUPT_PRIORITY asserts, saved context)", "FreeRTOS.org: Running the RTOS on an ARM Cortex-M Core (interrupt priorities); Customisation (FreeRTOSConfig.h)", "Arm Armv7-M ARM B3.3 SysTick (24-bit reload)"],
  "view": true,
  "layout": "custom",
  "agentOmit": ["view"]
}
